    {
      "id": "FDW-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-formal-weyl-limit",
      "title": "Compact Weyl dimension formula on U(p) × U(q) and shifted Vandermonde limit",
      "hypotheses": "Ambient rank N = p + q with p ≥ 1 positive signs and q ≥ 1 negative signs assigned by ε : {0, …, N − 1} → {+, −}; strictly decreasing Harish-Chandra parameter λ = (λ₀ > ⋯ > λ_{N−1}) with λ_a − (N − 1)/2 ∈ ℤ for all 0 ≤ a < N; compact and noncompact half-sums ρ_c, ρ_n; lowest compact K-types T_t of K ≃ U(p) × U(q) of highest weight Λ(t) = λ(t) + ρ_n − ρ_c along the integer ray λ_a(t) = λ_a + t(N − 1 − a) (t ∈ ℕ); and positive formal degrees d(λ), d(λ(t)) > 0 satisfying d(λ(t)) / V(λ(t)) = d(λ) / V(λ).",
      "statement": "Every irreducible unitary representation T of K ≃ U(p) × U(q) of highest weight Λ (integral and antitone on each sign block) has dimension [∏_{0≤a<b<N, ε_a=ε_b} ((Λ + ρ_c)_a − (Λ + ρ_c)_b)] / (F_p F_q); for 0 ≤ a < b < N with ε_a = ε_b, ρ_{n,a} − ρ_{n,b} = n_{a,b} := #{c : a < c < b, ε_c ≠ ε_a}, so at Λ = λ + ρ_n − ρ_c one has dim(T) = [∏_{a<b, ε_a=ε_b} (λ_a − λ_b + n_{a,b})] / (F_p F_q); along λ_a(t) = λ_a + t(N − 1 − a), Y_t = t^{pq} dim(T_t) / d(λ(t)) converges as t → ∞ to V(λ) / [d(λ) F_p F_q A] where A = ∏_{0≤b<a<N, ε_a≠ε_b} (a − b); and equating this limit with c π^{pq} / A for c = F_N / (π^{pq} F_p F_q) yields d(λ) = V(λ) / F_N.",
      "definitions": [
        "superfactorial product F_m = ∏_{0≤a<m} a! = ∏_{0≤a<b<m} (b − a) and Vandermonde product V(λ) = ∏_{0≤a<b<N} (λ_a − λ_b)",
        "sign-block order embeddings e_+ : {0, …, p − 1} → {0, …, N − 1} and e_− : {0, …, q − 1} → {0, …, N − 1} satisfying (ρ_c)_{e_±(i)} − (ρ_c)_{e_±(j)} = j − i",
        "intermediate opposite-sign index count n_{a,b} = #{c : a < c < b, ε_c ≠ ε_a} = ρ_{n,a} − ρ_{n,b} for same-sign pairs a < b"
      ],
