      "title": "Polar Haar measure calibration, Schur operator reduction, and Gaussian coefficient lower limit",
      "hypotheses": "Mixed signature (p, q) (p, q ≥ 1, N = p + q) with sign map ε, compact probability Haar measure dk on K ≃ U(p) × U(q), Hermitian off-diagonal noncompact tangent matrix P(z) (z ∈ ℂ^{pq}) with real eigenvalues μ_0(z), …, μ_{N−1}(z), hyperbolic Jacobian J(z) = ∏_{0≤a<b<N} shc(μ_a(z) − μ_b(z)), polar constant c = F_N / (π^{pq} F_p F_q), and discrete-series family (σ_t, H_t) along λ_a(t) = λ_a + t(N − 1 − a) (t ∈ ℕ) carrying formal degree d(λ(t)) > 0 on μ_CD = c μ_polar and isometric lowest K-type embeddings j_t : T_t → H_t whose unit highest-weight vectors w_t ∈ T_t admit smooth compact highest-weight Casimir-eigenvector realizations of eigenvalue ‖λ(t)‖² − ‖ρ‖².",
      "statement": "The polar Haar measure μ_CD = c J(z) dk dz has exponential-chart Lie-ball density c_Ω(N) = 1/[2^{N(N−1)/2} vol_0(U(N))] = F_N/[2^{N(N+1)/2} π^{N(N+1)/2}] and equals the canonical compact-dual Haar measure cd(p, q); for any discrete series (σ, H) of formal degree d > 0 with isometric K-type embedding j : T → H and unit vector w ∈ T, (dim T)² / d = c ∫_{ℂ^{pq}} ‖F_T(P(z))‖_HS² J(z) dz and c ∫_{ℂ^{pq}} |⟨w, F_T(P(z)) w⟩|² J(z) dz ≤ dim(T) / d; and along λ_a(t) = λ_a + t(N − 1 − a), ⟨w_t, F_{T_t}(P(t^{−1/2} y)) w_t⟩ → exp(−Q_0(y)/2) pointwise where Q_0(y) = ∑_{0≤b<a<N, ε_a≠ε_b} (a − b)|y_{a,b}|², giving lim inf_{t→∞} Y_t ≥ c ∫_{ℂ^{pq}} exp(−Q_0(y)) dy = c π^{pq} / A.",
      "definitions": [
        "Hermitian noncompact tangent matrix P(z) with P(z)_{a,b} = z_{a,b} for 0 ≤ b < a < N (ε_a ≠ ε_b), P(z)_{b,a} = conj(z_{a,b}), and zero same-sign entries",
        "hyperbolic Jacobian J(z) = ∏_{0≤a<b<N} shc(μ_a(z) − μ_b(z)) and compact-dual polar constant c = F_N / (π^{pq} F_p F_q)",
        "rescaled Gaussian quadratic form Q_0(y) = ∑_{0≤b<a<N, ε_a≠ε_b} (a − b)|y_{a,b}|² with ∫_{ℂ^{pq}} exp(−Q_0(y)) dy = π^{pq} / A"
